      "writtenOn": "2025-05-07T17:51:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This should have a return code, so the host can retry this if TZ got interrupted (by a non-secure interrupt or just yielded).\n\nThe way Trusty currently works (other TEEs might do things differently, I think some of them support yielding direct messages):\n* The VM availability messages are non-yielding direct messages (handled with interrupts disabled). Since it can\u0027t block, the handler just queues up work to be done later (top-half/bottom-half-style).\n* Trusty still needs cycles to do actual work. The direct message is followed by an `FFA_RUN` which _can_ be interrupted, so we need to run it as many times as needed.\n* We poll in between `FFA_RUN` calls to check whether the VM availability message has completed.",
      "revId": "3f52acc51e52460793d729815c7525273e7a46de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3345a91d_01dce3e0",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 87
      },
      "lineNbr": 259,
      "author": {
        "id": 1942270
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-12T14:27:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I get your point, it is tricky to retry calling an SMC from the hypervisor (which runs in non-preemptible context) without going back to the linux host. Without having some guarantees that this will succeed in the future, we can end up spinning forever.",
      "parentUuid": "6cab3da5_3a5bb13a",
      "revId": "3f52acc51e52460793d729815c7525273e7a46de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "703e66f0_06921c0c",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 87
      },
      "lineNbr": 314,
      "author": {
        "id": 1951687
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-07T16:42:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That smp_store_release does not look useful. This function is protected by a spinlock and no-one else is reading that vm_avail_bitmap.\n\nAlso we\u0027ve set already vm_avail_bitmap for all the SPs. Is there any point using that NOTIFIED_ALL?",
      "revId": "3f52acc51e52460793d729815c7525273e7a46de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "75703b62_ec6aa5bf",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 87
      },
      "lineNbr": 314,
      "author": {
        "id": 1809582
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-07T17:27:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e That smp_store_release does not look useful. This function is protected by a spinlock and no-one else is reading that vm_avail_bitmap.\n\nThere is one read of this variable that is not protected by the spinlock (or at least there was when I wrote it). If that\u0027s still there, do we not need the atomic store?\n\n\u003e Is there any point using that NOTIFIED_ALL?\n\nI figured using an exact value in a macro to set and check would be less error-prone than using `(1 \u003c\u003c num_vm_avail_sps) - 1` everywhere.",
      "parentUuid": "703e66f0_06921c0c",
      "revId": "3f52acc51e52460793d729815c7525273e7a46de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
