        "id": 1809582
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-07T17:51:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This should return `-EINTR` or `-EAGAIN` if the VM availability notification needs a retry.",
      "revId": "3f52acc51e52460793d729815c7525273e7a46de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9813a28f_19fae206",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 87
      },
      "lineNbr": 1167,
      "author": {
        "id": 1942270
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-12T14:27:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why do you require the VM availability (only creation msg) for the host ? What does Trusty do with it ? TBH I am in favor of dropping this to simplifying this code. Please feel free to re-open it.",
      "parentUuid": "713e1f7b_be7a3b85",
      "revId": "3f52acc51e52460793d729815c7525273e7a46de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1f64f407_bb821e53",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 87
      },
      "lineNbr": 1167,
      "author": {
        "id": 1809582
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-12T23:24:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From the perspective of the secure world, the host is a VM like any other.\n\nFor Trusty specifically, we only allow memory operations from VMs that we have seen a creation message. We reject operations from unknown VMs. That means we need a message for the host, unless we hard-code its ID as an exemption.",
      "parentUuid": "9813a28f_19fae206",
      "revId": "3f52acc51e52460793d729815c7525273e7a46de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "abb4e498_98c03a4f",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 87
      },
      "lineNbr": 1167,
      "author": {
        "id": 1809582
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-13T01:17:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After taking another look at this: if you can guarantee and write a comment that no NS interrupts are enabled here (e.g. the GIC hasn\u0027t been configured yet), then it might be safe to not restart the call.\n\nIt might still be worthwhile to check and `WARN_ON` the return code.",
      "parentUuid": "1f64f407_bb821e53",
      "revId": "3f52acc51e52460793d729815c7525273e7a46de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6d8d19b4_07122e2f",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 87
      },
      "lineNbr": 1167,
      "author": {
        "id": 1809582
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-13T02:42:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "On second thought, you should still check the result here and retry while it\u0027s `-EAGAIN` or `-EINTR`. Trusty will queue up the request and return `FFA_RET_RETRY` on the first attempt, so you always need to try at least a second time (with `FFA_RUN` in between).",
      "parentUuid": "abb4e498_98c03a4f",
      "revId": "3f52acc51e52460793d729815c7525273e7a46de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ec547022_e63bb480",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 87
      },
      "lineNbr": 1167,
      "author": {
        "id": 1942270
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-13T10:20:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`if you can guarantee and write a comment that no NS interrupts are enabled here (e.g. the GIC hasn\u0027t been configured yet),` - we cannot guarantee such a thing. The host can issue whenever it want the first FFA_VERSION call. \n\n`It might still be worthwhile to check and WARN_ON the return code.` - what\u0027s the behavior if this call is not implemented ? I don\u0027t want to get spurious `WARN_ON` on other devices.\n\n`On second thought, you should still check the result here and retry..` - yes I think we can retry this.",
      "parentUuid": "6d8d19b4_07122e2f",
      "revId": "3f52acc51e52460793d729815c7525273e7a46de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
