      },
      "lineNbr": 1167,
      "author": {
        "id": 1809582
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-13T16:11:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e we cannot guarantee such a thing. The host can issue whenever it want the first FFA_VERSION call.\n\nRight, my mistake. I thought you were calling this code from `hyp_ffa_init`. When you\u0027re piggybacking on an existing FF-A call, interrupts are very likely enabled.\n\n\u003e  what\u0027s the behavior if this call is not implemented ?\n\nIf an SP doesn\u0027t implement the creation message, it wouldn\u0027t be in its manifest, right? SPs have to explicitly opt into receiving these, and then it\u0027s not likely they\u0027ll return \"unimplemented\".",
      "parentUuid": "241cbd59_36d15c9f",
      "revId": "3f52acc51e52460793d729815c7525273e7a46de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8cf3acf6_07d8b178",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 87
      },
      "lineNbr": 1167,
      "author": {
        "id": 1809582
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-13T17:51:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After working around the `num_vm_avail_sps` issue locally, this call now goes into an infinite loop:\n```\nlong sm_ffa_handle_framework_msg(struct smc_ret18 *):585: Got VM creation message for 0\nlong sm_ffa_handle_framework_msg(struct smc_ret18 *):607: VM creation returning -7\nvoid sm_irq_return_ns(void):1020: got irq on cpu 3, stdcallcpu -1\nvoid sm_irq_return_ns(void):1028: got irq on cpu 3, return -14\nlong sm_ffa_handle_framework_msg(struct smc_ret18 *):585: Got VM creation message for 0\nlong sm_ffa_handle_framework_msg(struct smc_ret18 *):607: VM creation returning -7\nvoid sm_irq_return_ns(void):1020: got irq on cpu 3, stdcallcpu -1\nvoid sm_irq_return_ns(void):1028: got irq on cpu 3, return -14\nlong sm_ffa_handle_framework_msg(struct smc_ret18 *):585: Got VM creation message for 0\n[...]\n```\n\nWe need to either return all the way to the host so the NS interrupt can be handled, _or_ alternatively not send the message for the host. The latter comes with its own complications, so we should discuss this further.",
      "parentUuid": "8e1e76ed_c951bd42",
      "revId": "3f52acc51e52460793d729815c7525273e7a46de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "091eb019_c1d78d48",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 87
      },
      "lineNbr": 1167,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-13T17:56:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think _not_ sending the message for the host is spec compliant. How would the SP know that there is a host at vm-id 1 that don\u0027t get a creation message?",
      "parentUuid": "8cf3acf6_07d8b178",
      "revId": "3f52acc51e52460793d729815c7525273e7a46de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d34410b6_eebc12e2",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 87
      },
      "lineNbr": 1167,
